0.50 w 56.00 539.89 m 539.28 539.89 l S
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 522.89 Td (Mechanics is the branch of physics that studies motion and the causes of motion. Kinematics) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 508.89 Td (describes motion without discussing forces. In this unit, we describe how position changes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 494.89 Td (with time using distance, displacement, velocity, and acceleration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 475.89 Td (Motion can occur in one dimension, such as a car moving along a straight road, or in two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 461.89 Td (dimensions, such as a ball thrown through the air. The same basic ideas apply, but two-) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 447.89 Td (dimensional motion is handled by breaking the motion into perpendicular components.) Tj ET
