BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 304.89 Td (One-dimensional motion occurs along a straight line. Examples include an elevator moving up) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 290.89 Td (and down, a train on a straight track, or a stone dropped from rest. The direction of motion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 276.89 Td (can be represented using positive and negative signs.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 56.00 253.89 Td (Uniform Motion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 236.89 Td (Uniform motion means velocity is constant. The acceleration is zero, and equal displacements) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 222.89 Td (are covered in equal time intervals.) Tj ET
q 0.95 g 56.00 186.89 483.28 24.00 re f Q
