BT /F2 12 Tf 56.00 165.89 Td (Uniformly Accelerated Motion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 148.89 Td (Uniformly accelerated motion means acceleration is constant. Velocity changes by equal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56.00 134.89 Td (amounts in equal time intervals. The equations of motion are used for this case.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 62.00 115.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 76.00 115.89 Td (A car speeding up uniformly has constant positive acceleration.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 62.00 98.89 Td (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 76.00 98.89 Td (A ball thrown upward has constant downward acceleration due to gravity.) Tj ET
